      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Linear data structures include Arrays, Linked Lists, Stacks, and Queues.",
        "Trees cover properties, traversal algorithms, and special tree variants.",
        "Graph representations and standard traversal algorithms are critical for modeling networks.",
        "Algorithm design techniques structure the approaches used for searching and sorting.",
        "Complexity analysis uses Big-O notation to measure algorithm time and space performance."
